-- title:
--   Relabelling by γ∈Γ(ℓ')∩Γ₀(M') fixes a supersingular class
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a non-zero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. The ambient data, summarised here as four groups, are: (i) reduction data at $q$ — a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, a finite set $W$ of places of the subfield $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-Laurent series generated by the $j$-series and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion, assumed to be exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine-geometric, with value at the geometric $j$-generator in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$), the inclusion of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, a constant reduction $R_0$ of the former onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ whose residue map is compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$, and a chosen element $s\in W$; (ii) small-field data — an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ and algebraically closed residue field, every element of $A$ being congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$; (iii) auxiliary level data — a prime $\ell'\neq q$ with $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$, a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity $\xi\in k_0$ admitting a ring embedding $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending it to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the $k_0$-base change $K$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$, and a non-zero $j\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$; (iv) moduli package over $A_0$ — variable-change equivariance $h_\ell$ of level-$\ell'$ Katz structures and $h_M$ of $\Gamma_0(p^k)$ kernel polynomials, group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models with unit discriminant which are chord–tangent and have the origin as identity, a Drinfeld level transport $\mathcal T$ at $q$ which is a section transport, and the realisability of variable changes and of coefficient maps by graded ring homomorphisms of the projective model rings. Let $\kappa$ be the residue field of $A_0$. Then, for every raw datum $x$ for $\mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,h_\ell\,h_M\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$ over $\kappa$ — a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with unit discriminant, together with a family of $\Gamma_0$-kernel polynomials for the prime powers dividing $M'$, a level-$\ell'$ Katz pair and a raw Drinfeld pair, all satisfying the corresponding level conditions — if the only point $P$ of the affine curve of $x$ with $q\cdot P=0$ is $0$, then for every $\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\c&d\end{pmatrix}\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying both in $\Gamma(\ell')$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every raw datum $x_1$ of the same type and every witness that the discriminant of the curve underlying the Drinfeld-pair component of $x$ is a unit: if $x_1$ has the same curve and the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-component as $x$, its Katz pair is the $\gamma$-relabelling $(aP+cQ,\,bP+dQ)$ of that of $x$ computed in the group of affine points, and its Drinfeld pair is the corresponding $\gamma$-relabelling of that of $x$ computed with the group law $\mathcal G$, then $x_1$ and $x$ have the same class in the quotient $\mathrm{Pt}(\kappa)$ of raw data by the variable-change relation.
--
--   This is the rigidity of level structures at a supersingular point in the form needed here: on a curve over the algebraically closed residue field with no non-trivial $q$-torsion, relabelling the Drinfeld basis at $q$ and the Katz pair at $\ell'$ by a matrix that is trivial modulo $\ell'$ and upper-triangular modulo $M'$ does not change the isomorphism class of the datum. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAut_sub_self_mem_of_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_Gamma_of_over_ssPlace_rigidDataPow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAut_sub_self_mem_of_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_Gamma_of_over_ssPlace_rigidDataPow) in the study of level automorphisms over the supersingular fibre.
